    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-071 — Inline Routing, Culling Regression, and Async Logging.** Fixes the two most stubborn rendering bugs of the session:\n1. **Wikipedia headings invisible** (blank bands where `History`, `Markup`, `HTML5` should be).\n2. **Blank page on scroll** (any scroll past ~641px).\n\n## The Three Bugs\n\n1. **Inline Routing:** MediaWiki's Vector 2022 sets `<h2>` to `display: inline` inside `.mw-heading`. Our `layout_block_children` blindly treated all children as blocks, giving the `<h2>` a local `y=0`.\n2. **Viewport Collapse:** Initial `on_draw` fired before GTK allocated the window (`viewport_h=0`), collapsing percentage heights.\n3. **Culling Regression:** `paint_children` culled `Box` nodes by their own height. `<body>` was clamped to `641px`, so scrolling past `641px` culled the entire body and its `30440px` of children.\n\n## The Fixes\n\n- **Inline Routing:** `layout_block_children` routes `display: inline` to `inline_run`. Flushes at the end of the loop.\n- **Culling:** Restored ADR-069 rule — only cull `Text` / `InlineContext`. `Box` is always recursed.\n- **Viewport Guard:** `on_draw` returns early if `viewport_h <= 0`.\n\n## Async Logging Upgrade\n\nSynchronous `fprintf` during paint caused the compositor to blank the window, hiding the bug. We upgraded ADR-046's logger to an **asynchronous background thread**. Added `LayoutDetail` / `PaintDetail` categories and hooked `log_shutdown()` into `main.cpp`.\n\n## Verified\n\n| Check | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Wikipedia h2 headings | Invisible | **Visible** |\n| Scroll past 641px | Blank page | **Smooth** |\n| Initial viewport | Collapsed | Renders correctly |\n| Logging | Blocks UI | Non-blocking |\n\n## Verification category\n\n**Production-visual, end-to-end.**\n\nRefs #277\n",
